ation with the Harvard School of Public Health, again as valedictorian. He later completed a master’s degree in environmental policy at Cambridge University, UK. During his studies he received multiple national and international scholarships, including the prestigious PEXIM Cambridge Scholarship.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>From 2012 to 2017 he served as a health advisor to the Prime Minister of the Republic of Macedonia and was the initiator and chief expert consultant of the national healthy nutrition campaign “Health is a Choice!”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>His interest in nutrition began immediately after medical school. Through studying epigenetic environmental influences, he focused on gene–environment interaction, especially nutrigenetics.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Today he continues to follow the latest scientific research on how lifestyle — particularly nutrition and physical activity — affects disease and its treatment. His work is dedicated to translating modern medical science into practical guidance and concrete advice for patients.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','BOOK PROMOTION – “GUIDE TO LONGEVITY” BY DR. MITOV – 17.07.2018 (TUESDAY) 8 PM','','inherit','closed','closed','','1173-revision-v1','','','2026-02-13 23:52:46','2026-02-13 23:52:46','',1173,'https://user17.delovna.finki.ukim.mk/?p=1174',0,'revision','',0);
