лов, коишто прифатија да бидат генерални покровители на оваа колонија и воедно овој нов духовен конак на уметноста кој со текот на времето се претвара во годишна традиција на уметниците од Радовиш.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Големиот Винсент Ван Гог рекол дека големите нешта не се создаваат по импулс, туку по пат на серија од малите нешта кои се обединуваат. Токму тоа беше и целта на започнувањето на ваквите колонии – да се обединат уметници од Македонија со уметници од повеќе страни на светот. Во таа смисла помеѓу учесниците на Третата Меѓународна Ликовна колонија беа уметници од неколку генерации ликовни уметници од Македонија помеѓу кои и доајените на македонската уметност: Новица Трајковски, Владимир Темков, Ангел Коруновски, Стефан Хаџи-Николов, Цветанка Јованова Хермес, Мирослав Трендафиловски – Мики и Запро Запров. Исто така во колонијата учествуваа и уметници од странство меѓу кои: Летив Намдагжанчивин – Ли од Монголија, Евгени Петров од Бугарија и Мита Ристиќ од Србија, како и членови на ДЛУР Рада, Радовиш: Марјан Крстев, Крсте Тарабунов, Душан Коцев и Ѓорге Атанасов…“</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Изложбата во Куманово ќе биде поставена до 22.01.2019 .</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','ИЗЛОЖБА “ТРЕТА МЕЃУНАРОДНА РАДОВИШКА ЛИКОВНА КОЛОНИЈА – СВЕТИ ЃЕОРЃИЈ 2018“ РАДОВИШ – 27.12.2018 (ЧЕТВРТОК) ИЗЛОЖБЕН САЛОН 18.30ч.','','inherit','closed','closed','','1375-revision-v1','','','2026-02-14 19:09:23','2026-02-14 19:09:23','',1375,'https://user17.delovna.finki.ukim.mk/?p=1377',0,'revision','',0);
INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (1378,1,'2026-02-14 19:10:02','2026-02-14 19:10:02','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>21/12/2018</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/telop-RADOVIS.jpg\" alt=\"\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>EXHIBITION “THIRD INTERNATIONAL RADOVIŠ ART COLONY – ST. GEORGE 2018” RADOVIŠ – 27.12.2018 (THURSDAY) EXHIBITION SALON 18:30<br>21/12/2018</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Exhibition of paintings from the International Radoviš Art Colony<br>“St. George 2018” in Kumanovo</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>On 27.12.2018 (Thursday) starting at 18:30, at the Exhibition Salon of the National Institution Center for Culture “Trajko Prokopiev” – Kumanovo, an exhibition of paintings from the International Radoviš Art Colony “St. George 2018” will be opened. The exhibition catalog states:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>“…The desire of visual artists from the Municipality of Radoviš to establish and participate in a true art colony — after more than fifty years of artistic tradition and the existence of the Association of Visual Artists of Radoviš, founded in 1966 — has in recent years been realized and nurtured as a continuing tradition of organizing art colonies where artists have the opportunity to create outstanding works. The joint efforts of the president of the Association of Visual Artists DLUR Rada Radoviš, Dušan Kocev, together with the organizing committee of the Third International Art Colony, the municipal councilors, the director of the Center for Culture Aco Karamanov – Radoviš, and many academic artists, resulted in the renewed holding of the colony. With this act, the monastery complex St. George shone on the spiritual and cultural map of visual art in the world.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>All of this would not have been possible without the support of the Municipality of Radoviš, together with Mayor Gerasim Konzulov and the Municipal Council, as well as the strong support of the Bučim Mine and its executive director Nikolajčo Nikolov, who accepted to be general patrons of this colony and of this new spiritual home of art, which over time is becoming an annual tradition for Radoviš artists.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The great Vincent van Gogh said that great things are not created by impulse, but through a series of small things brought together. That was precisely the goal of establishing such colonies — to unite artists from Macedonia with artists from various parts of the world. Among the participants of the Third International Art Colony were artists from several generations from Macedonia, including leading figures of Macedonian art: Novica Trajkovski, Vladimir Temkov, Angel Korunovski, Stefan Hadži-Nikolov, Cvetanka Jovanova Hermes, Miroslav Trendafilovski – Miki, and Zapro Zaprov. The colony also included international artists such as Letiv Namdagjanchivin – Li from Mongolia, Evgeni Petrov from Bulgaria, and Mita Ristić from Serbia, as well as members of DLUR Rada Radoviš: Marjan Krstev, Krste Tarabunov, Dušan Kocev, and Gjorgje Atanasov…”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The exhibition in Kumanovo will remain on display until 22.01.2019.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','EXHIBITION “THIRD INTERNATIONAL RADOVIŠ ART COLONY – ST. GEORGE 2018” RADOVIŠ – 27.12.2018 (THURSDAY) EXHIBITION SALON 18:30','','publish','open','open','','exhibition-third-international-radovis-art-colony-st-george-2018-radovis-27-12-2018-thursday-exhibition-salon-1830','','','2026-02-14 19:10:03','2026-02-14 19:10:03','',0,'https://user17.delovna.finki.ukim.mk/?p=1378',0,'post','',0);
INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (1379,1,'2026-02-14 19:10:02','2026-02-14 19:10:02','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>21/12/2018</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/telop-RADOVIS.jpg\" alt=\"\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>EXHIBITION “THIRD INTERNATIONAL RADOVIŠ ART COLONY – ST. GEORGE 2018” RADOVIŠ – 27.12.2018 (THURSDAY) EXHIBITION SALON 18:30<br>21/12/2018</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Exhibition of paintings from the International Radoviš Art Colony<br>“St. George 2018” in Kumanovo</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>On 27.12.2018 (Thursday) starting at 18:30, at the Exhibition Salon of the National Institution Center for Culture “Trajko Prokopiev” – Kumanovo, an exhibition of paintings from the International Radoviš Art Colony “St. George 2018” will be opened. The exhibition catalog states:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>“…The desire of visual artists from the Municipality of Radoviš to establish and participate in a true art colony — after more than fifty years of artistic tradition and the existence of the Association of Visual Artists of Radoviš, founded in 1966 — has in recent years been realized and nurtured as a continuing tradition of organizing art colonies where artists have the opportunity to create outstanding works. The joint efforts of the president of the Association of Visual Artists DLUR Rada Radoviš, Dušan Kocev, together with the organizing committee of the Third International Art Colony, the municipal councilors, the director of the Center for Culture Aco Karamanov – Radoviš, and many academic artists, resulted in the renewed holding of the colony. With this act, the monastery complex St. George shone on the spiritual and cultural map of visual art in the world.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>All of this would not have been possible without the support of the Municipality of Radoviš, together with Mayor Gerasim Konzulov and the Municipal Council, as well as the strong support of the Bučim Mine and its executive director Nikolajčo Nikolov, who accepted to be general patrons of this colony and of this new spiritual home of art, which over time is becoming an annual tradition for Radoviš artists.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The great Vincent van Gogh said that great things are not created by impulse, but through a series of small things brought together. That was precisely the goal of establishing such colonies — to unite artists from Macedonia with artists from various parts of the world. Among the participants of the Third International Art Colony were artists from several generations from Macedonia, including leading figures of Macedonian art: Novica Trajkovski, Vladimir Temkov, Angel Korunovski, Stefan Hadži-Nikolov, Cvetanka Jovanova Hermes, Miroslav Trendafilovski – Miki, and Zapro Zaprov. The colony also included international artists such as Letiv Namdagjanchivin – Li from Mongolia, Evgeni Petrov from Bulgaria, and Mita Ristić from Serbia, as well as members of DLUR Rada Radoviš: Marjan Krstev, Krste Tarabunov, Dušan Kocev, and Gjorgje Atanasov…”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The exhibition in Kumanovo will remain on display until 22.01.2019.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','EXHIBITION “THIRD INTERNATIONAL RADOVIŠ ART COLONY – ST. GEORGE 2018” RADOVIŠ – 27.12.2018 (THURSDAY) EXHIBITION SALON 18:30','','inherit','closed','closed','','1378-revision-v1','','','2026-02-14 19:10:02','2026-02-14 19:10:02','',1378,'https://user17.delovna.finki.ukim.mk/?p=1379',0,'revision','',0);
