act “entrance” into the artist’s intimacy, with symbols of vaults and arches recalling ancient Macedonian and Balkan roots, his works offer a return to spiritual wealth in a world of distorted values dominated by social media. His paintings evoke feelings that cannot simply be photographed but must be experienced. He positions the artist as a dissident voice against consumerism and artificial productivity.<br>— Kirila Cvetkovska, art historian</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>11,000 Days of Metamorphosis</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For Robert Cvetkovski, the artwork is like nature — full of waves, color, and matter. From today’s perspective, his art relates to abstract expressionism and non-figurative painting, yet he sees himself primarily as an author devoted to authenticity rather than styles or movements. His path moves from experimentation and symbolic figuration through expressive abstraction toward pure energetic and emotional expression where the figure disappears entirely.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>He immerses himself in the unreal and becomes part of the painting, which simultaneously emerges from him. The painting is not manufactured — it self-creates through the artist. Inner energy and core human emotions are materialized in the work and then dematerialized in the viewer’s perception, re-igniting the same impulses. Opposites are central: change and transience, fear and light, cold and warmth.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Layers of paint resemble fossil traces of emotional states — joy, love, anger, fear. His works often suggest a lyrical abstract landscape: misty twilight, trembling light, or an in-between space between dream and waking. Symbols and signs bind these fragments into a unified whole and guide them through the motif of the vault — the vault above us, within us, in the temple, the womb, the earth — the origin and the core.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The message has been sent and transcends language barriers.<br>Keep your receivers on.<br>— Gjorgji Kostovski, art historian</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','EXHIBITION – ROBERT CVETKOVSKI – PAINTINGS – “MESSAGE” – 21.11.2019 (THURSDAY) EXHIBITION SALON 20:00','','inherit','closed','closed','','1479-revision-v1','','','2026-02-14 19:38:04','2026-02-14 19:38:04','',1479,'https://user17.delovna.finki.ukim.mk/?p=1480',0,'revision','',0);
