lock-image\"><img src=\"http://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/279699590_3194016807549645_2816815251858691005_n-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5121\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":5120} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"http://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/279692513_3194015700883089_5733437929742566404_n-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5120\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":5119} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"http://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/279692492_3194017380882921_5212699498175102400_n-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5119\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":5118} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"http://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/279687666_3194017500882909_4589652222134172784_n-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5118\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":5117} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"http://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/279683736_3194016860882973_8954272302100115152_n-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5117\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->','Exhibition “Home Atmosphere” – Deјvid Stoilkovski','','publish','open','open','','exhibition-home-atmosphere-de%d1%98vid-stoilkovski','','','2026-02-14 21:06:39','2026-02-14 21:06:39','',0,'https://user17.delovna.finki.ukim.mk/?p=1575',0,'post','',0);
INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (1576,1,'2026-02-14 21:06:39','2026-02-14 21:06:39','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>17/05/2022</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Dejvid.jpg\" alt=\"\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Deјvid Stoilkovski, born in Kumanovo in 1997, lives and works in Kumanovo. He graduated from the Academy of Fine Arts in Skopje, Department of Graphics, in the class of Professor Slavica Janešlieva, and is currently pursuing master’s studies in painting under Jovan Šumkovski.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>He most enjoys creating murals, graffiti, and canvas paintings, but from time to time also explores other techniques and artistic directions. He has participated in multiple group exhibitions in Macedonia and Croatia.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>He is a co-organizer and participant in graffiti festivals in Kumanovo and has painted murals in cities across Macedonia as well as in the USA, Austria, and Montenegro.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>He first encountered art through graffiti drawing in Kumanovo as a child around 2010–2011, and year by year his interest and desire for graffiti to remain his way of life grew stronger. Over time, clear progress can be seen from amateur graffiti to the development of his own lettering style within graffiti culture and recognition among street art enthusiasts. Later, he enrolled at the Academy of Fine Arts in Skopje, Department of Graphics, where his style and direction of expression began to change. During the first two years of study he focused on abstract forms through printmaking, which was a completely new path in his life. In the following two years, abstraction blended with the opposite direction — hyperrealism — where he began painting murals on smaller surfaces to explore that approach, which opened many opportunities and led him to create more serious murals on larger surfaces.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This first solo exhibition is a collection of works spanning his periods from graffiti, through various artistic movements, to more recent mural painting. The works in the exhibition were created during 2020, 2021, and early 2022. The title “Home Atmosphere” refers to the figurative objects present in the works, which express nostalgia and a connection to home and family. If the figurative elements are removed, the compositions are reduced to pure abstract color fields in several shades. This exhibition can be seen as an overture to the artist’s further exploration of hyperrealism in mural and canvas painting.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":5148} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"http://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/280189987_3194015750883084_6617239365599239231_n-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5148\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":5147} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"http://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/280135931_3194015890883070_4744851420050490190_n-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5147\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":5146} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"http://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/280095391_3194016900882969_5825944291367840423_n-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5146\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":5145} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"http://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/280071263_3194017300882929_8252389357951003108_n-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5145\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":5144} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"http://nucktrajkoprokopiev.mk/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/280066769_3